{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And they came, etc., at evening.</b> The reason for this is to provide an opportunity for Lot to take them in and earn merit through their rescue. And although the Sages said (Genesis Rabbah 50:11) that he was saved in the merit of Abraham, still it was necessary to find him some merit of his own. For had they come by day, it is possible that the men of the city would not have allowed him to take them in at all." "<b>And Lot saw — and he rose, etc.</b> Meaning: he recognized in them that they were among those known to him as ministers of the Most High from when he dwelt in the neighborhood of Abraham. And this is what the verse means by <b>וַיַּרְא</b> — therefore he risked his life for them against the men of the city, and rose to meet them. And he said to them <b>ורחצו רגליכם</b> (\"wash your feet\"), for such was Abraham's custom with his guests, and he followed in his footsteps. And it was written in the Torah to inform us of the difference between Abraham and Lot, as they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 50:4): this one preceded washing, and that one preceded lodging before washing — for he was not insistent about their entering his house while still bearing idolatry, unlike Abraham, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:20.115114418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}